 "answer": "Assuming you mean **Jurong, Singapore: I’d exercise indoors right now.** At about **12:45 pm on October 17**, the latest West-region reading I could verify was **206 µg/m³ of 1-hour PM₂.₅ at noon**—in Singapore’s **High** band. The West region includes Jurong East and Jurong West. ([hazenow.app](https://hazenow.app/singapore/west))\n\nSingapore’s National Environment Agency advises **healthy people to avoid strenuous outdoor activity** when the reading is High. Children, pregnant people, older adults, and people with chronic heart or lung disease should **avoid outdoor activity for the next hour**. Check the West-region 1-hour PM₂.₅ reading again before heading out; haze levels can change quickly. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
